Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28, no IPv6 and no CA
bundle. q2-applemusic runs from the card's .applemusic folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's
patch/addon.c): Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, starts it from that row, draws its page and keeps the
Q2 awake while it downloads. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.applemusic, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-applemusic-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .applemusic/run: q2-applemusic copied to /tmp and run there in a
               restart loop
  q2app        installed as .applemusic/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Apple Music,
               search=Search Apple Music)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               installed beside it: Streaming's row icon, 52 px (Legacy) and 40 px (iPod), a white
               note on Apple Music's red, in Q2 Pod's style
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Install
-------

Q2 Pod's System settings -> Apps installs the latest release over Wi-Fi. By hand, unzip
q2-applemusic-*.zip from https://github.com/group-a-study/q2-applemusic/releases/latest to the
card's root with the Q2 powered off. See the top-level README.md.

Build
-----

  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh [OUT]

Go 1.22 or later and python3. The binary is CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=mipsle GOMIPS=softfloat,
static, so it needs none of the Q2's libraries and the firmware's -mfp64 doesn't matter. It uses Go's
standard library alone. Tests: go test ./... (a fake Apple behind the HTTP transport) and
python3 contrib/shanlingq2/test_launcher.py. A tag q2-vX.Y matching cmd/q2-applemusic/main.go's
version publishes the release (.github/workflows/release.yml); System settings -> Apps takes its
only ZIP.

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.applemusic/run when Streaming's Apple Music row is pressed and it
isn't running. The launcher copies q2-applemusic and itself to /tmp and leaves the card at once, so
USB storage can always take the card; the loop restarts it after a failure, waiting 5 s and doubling
to a minute, runs it at nice 10 (playback and the Q2's pages first), and leaves its pid in
/tmp/q2-applemusic. A TERM to it ends q2-applemusic cleanly: the song under way is dropped (its
.part files removed) and the queue saved; one still there 15 s later is killed. Q2 Pod sends it for
Stop Streaming Services, Home's Rockbox row, an Apps update or remove, and USB storage (after which
it starts it again). With nothing to download and its page unused for 15 minutes, q2-applemusic
stops by itself; a stream session waiting for the Q2 to play on keeps it going (for an hour without
the Q2 moving on). It writes no log: Not Downloaded.txt, the songs that failed, is the only report
it leaves.

  /tmp/q2-applemusic.state
      hold=1 while a song downloads or streams in (Q2 Pod holds standby off) and version; while not
      signed in with a subscription, also the sign-in page's addr, pin, qr, qrsize and note, for Q2
      Pod's QR code page
  /tmp/q2-applemusic.sock
      datagrams: q quits
  /tmp/q2-applemusic.browse.sock
      Q2SPOT/1 (q2-pod's docs/librespot.md) for the Q2's page, below
  /tmp/q2-applemusic.play, /tmp/q2-applemusic.playing
      Stream mode (below): "<seq> <folder>", the session Q2 Pod plays; and the path of the song it
      plays from it, which Q2 Pod writes
  port 8100 (the next free one if taken)
      the sign-in page: /?k=KEY signs a browser in (the key is the QR code's, new each start),
      POST /api/login takes the PIN, POST /api/token checks and saves a media-user-token (the value,
      a Cookie header or a cookies.txt), POST /api/signout removes it; posts need the header X-Q2: 1
  .applemusic/media-user-token, .applemusic/organize, .applemusic/mode, .applemusic/queue.json,
  .applemusic/bulk.json, .applemusic/failed.json
      the sign-in, Organize Files (on, off), Mode (download, stream), the songs waiting, Download
      All's lists to go and the songs that failed; updates keep them
  Apple Music/Not Downloaded.txt
      the songs that failed, for a computer (Downloads, below)
  .applemusic/devtoken
      the web player's developer token, read from music.apple.com's script and kept until it
      expires or Apple refuses it
  .applemusic/device.wvd
      optional: a Widevine device (pywidevine's .wvd) to use instead of the built-in one
  .applemusic/stream/<seq>/
      Stream mode's songs, none kept past the next session

The media-user-token is the account's sign-in: treat it like a password. One line in
.applemusic/media-user-token, put there by hand, works too. So does a cookies file (cookies.go): a
*cookie*.txt at the card's root, in Apple Music/ or in .applemusic/, looked for at the start and
every 10 s; its music.apple.com media-user-token (a Netscape cookies.txt line, #HttpOnly_ or not,
or a Cookie header) is checked with Apple, saved if it signs in with a subscription, and the file
deleted (a browser's export can hold the Apple ID's myacinfo too). One Apple refuses stays, the
menu saying why, and is asked about again only once it changes (size or time). It lasts months; when Apple refuses it
(403 on the account), the page asks to sign in again. Apple not answering at all is told apart from
a refused token (apple.IsNoNetwork, apple.ErrSignedOut), so a dropped Wi-Fi never asks for a new one.
A refused developer token (401) is read again from music.apple.com once, then the request retried.

HTTPS is checked against Mozilla's CA bundle, which the app carries (internal/tlsroots, from curl's
conversion); the firmware has none. On a Q2 whose clock was never set, certificates are checked at
the time a plain HTTP Date header gives.

The page
--------

Each row's kind says what a press does (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): list opens a level, action sends an
op and toasts its reply, search opens the Q2's keyboard, remote opens the QR code, local plays from
the card (a song: its folder from it; a folder ending /: its songs listed; context album: in track
order), info does nothing. A row's position is the op Play/Pause held sends.

  menu
      Downloaded Songs, Recently Added, Songs, Playlists, Albums, Artists, Search Apple Music,
      Downloads, Mode, Organize Files, Account, Stop Apple Music; signed out, Sign In from Your
      Phone. From the sign-in as last found (it never waits on Apple); refresh
  recent, playlists, albums, artists
      list rows: tracks <list> (Play/Pause held: download <list>), or artist <id>; playlists and
      albums start with Download All Playlists / Download All Albums (bulk playlists|albums)
  artist <id>
      a library artist's (r.…) albums in the library; a catalogue artist's Top Songs, then its
      albums, singles and EPs
  tracks <list>
      Download All (or All on the card; in Stream mode Play All, stream <list>, first), then each
      song: local when on the card, else download <list>#<id>, or in Stream mode stream
      <list>#<id> (Play/Pause held still downloads); refresh
  search <term>, found <kind>:<term>
      songs, albums, artists and playlists of one catalogue search, 25 each, kept two minutes
  download <list> or <list>#<id>
      queues the list's songs not on the card (or that one); its message says how many
  bulk albums|playlists
      Download All: every library album or playlist, queued one list at a time (Downloads, below)
  stream <list> or <list>#<id>
      plays the list from its first song (or that one) in a new stream session
  downloads
      the queue; cancel <key>, cancelall, retry [<key>], clearfailed, bulkstop
  cardartists, cardalbums <artist>
      Downloaded Songs with Artist/Album folders on the card: the songs in Apple Music/ itself
      (Unsorted Songs), then each artist's folder, Playlists among them, then 48 kHz and Higher
      (cardartists 48khz, its artists as cardalbums 48khz/<artist>); an artist's albums, oldest
      first, each a local folder row with context album
  mode, organize, account, signout, stop
      Mode download or stream; Organize Files on or off; the account (subscription, country) and
      Sign Out; the token removed; the app stopped

Lists of songs are named songs (the library's), chart, album:<id> (l.… a library album, its songs
in the library; else the catalogue's), playlist:<id> (p.… a library playlist; pl.… the
catalogue's), artisttop:<id> and search:<term>; they are fetched whole (Apple's pages of 100,
following each page's next, at most 5,000 songs) and kept two minutes, so a download takes the
songs as the page showed them. A library song is its catalogue song (playParams.catalogId); one
with none (uploaded to the library) is left out. Cursors are offsets, read from a request's last
argument. A request waits at most 8 s for its list (Q2 Pod waits 15 s): a list still coming answers
one info row, Loading..., with the message refresh, so the page asks again every 2 s while the one
fetch carries on; a list past its two minutes is shown as kept while it is fetched again. At most
two fetches run at once.

Downloads
---------

As gamdl's aac-web: for each song, the playback service (webPlayback, salableAdamId) gives its
tags (the asset's metadata: title, artists, album, numbers, date, genre, composer, copyright, the
explicit flag) and its AAC 256 kbps stream (flavor 28:ctrp256), an HLS playlist of one fragmented
MP4 in byte ranges, joined into one request (a dropped connection resumed with a range; one silent
for a minute dropped and resumed). Its samples are encrypted with CENC (AES-CTR, an IV each, in
senc): the first fragments' sample description (the first seconds) with Apple's fixed prefetch
key, the rest's with the song's, whose key ID the playlist's Widevine EXT-X-KEY names (not the
default one, skd's s1/e1, which every playlist lists first). internal/widevine asks for that key: a
signed license request (pywidevine's format: the device's client identification in the clear,
RSASSA-PSS with SHA-1) to acquireWebPlaybackLicense, whose license's session key (RSA-OAEP) and
the keys derived from it (AES-CMAC, as OEMCrypto) check its HMAC and unwrap the content key. Each
sample description takes the key its tenc names (or, as gamdl, the prefetch key for the first of
two). The stream is fetched to <name>.m4a.enc.part beside its name, then each sample decrypted
into <name>.m4a.part: ftyp M4A, a moov (the stream's mvhd, tkhd, mdhd and hdlr with the real
duration, its edit list for the encoder's priming, one sample description as mp4a with no sinf,
stts, stsc, stsz and stco in chunks of 44 samples, about a second each, as iTunes writes them),
then one mdat; renamed into place. A stream of 48 kHz or more (its sample description's rate), which
iPods skip on, goes in Apple Music/48khz/ instead, always as <album artist>/<year> - <album>/ (a
playlist's as Playlists/<playlist>/), the folder chosen once the stream is read: the encrypted
stream waits in Apple Music/ itself. Apple's web stream is 44.1 kHz, so this is a safety net. The tags are iTunes atoms in moov/udta/meta/ilst (©nam, ©ART, aART, ©alb,
©gen, ©day, ©wrt, cprt, trkn, disk, cpil, rtng, cnID, stik, covr, ©lyr), as TagLib reads them: the
cover (600 px JPEG), and the lyrics when Apple has them (catalog songs/<id>/lyrics, TTML): timed by
line, as LRC, "[01:03.01]A line" a line; else the plain text, a blank line between verses. Q2 Pod
shows them in Now Playing. One song downloads at a time, two seconds apart. Offline, signed out,
without a subscription or with the card away, the queue waits and tries again every 30 s. Any other
failure is the song's: it is tried again three times, 5, 10 and 15 s apart (Downloads says "try 2 of
4"), then joins the failed songs and the queue goes on. The failed songs are kept in
.applemusic/failed.json (across restarts) and listed in Apple Music/Not Downloaded.txt, written
before the queue moves on: two lines of explanation, a header, then a tab-separated line each with
the song's artist, album, title, the playlist it came from, the reason, its music.apple.com/<country>/
song/<id> link (gamdl takes it) and when. Try the Failed Again queues them; a song queued again
leaves both files, and with none left they go. Clear the Failed empties them.

Download All (bulk albums|playlists): the library's albums or playlists, as the page listed them,
go in .applemusic/bulk.json. Once no song waits, the next list's songs are fetched and queued (a
list gone from the library is skipped), so Apple is asked for one list at a time and the queue
stays one album long. Downloads says how many lists are left; Stop Download All drops them, the
songs queued still downloading.

A playlist's songs (playlist:<id>, however downloaded) are kept as an album of their own, in
Apple Music/Playlists/<playlist>/, "07 - Title [id].m4a" by the song's place in the playlist:
tagged with the playlist's name as their album, Playlists as their album artist, that place as
their number (of the playlist's length), and as a compilation; each keeps its own cover. The
folder holds the playlist's cover as cover.jpg (600 px), Q2 Pod's picture for the album in
Coverflow and Albums, and .q2-playlist, its id and the album's name: a playlist renamed since
keeps its folder and album; another playlist of the same name gets "<name> (2)". A song is on the
card once per album it was downloaded into: the queue knows a playlist's songs by the playlist and
the song (pp.…:<id>), other songs by the song.

A song listed in an album (album:<id>) carries the album (apple.AlbumRef: a library album's name and
artist, with its catalogue album's year and cover, include=catalog). When the playback service puts
the song on another album (sameAlbum: titles compared without case, punctuation, bracketed editions
or " - EP"/" - Single"), as for a library compilation Apple matched to the songs' own releases, the
song is filed and tagged as the listed album: its name and artist, year and cover, the library's
track number of the album's length, a compilation for Various Artists. Such a song counts as on the
card only in that album's folder (onCard: a copy in a folder named as the album, or in Apple Music/
itself), so it downloads into the compilation though its own album has it; once saved, a copy of it
alone in its own album's folder (how v1.6 and before filed it) is deleted, with the folders left
empty. Every other song is filed by its own tags, as before.

Organize Files on (the default, .applemusic/organize missing or anything but "off"): a song goes
in Apple Music/<album artist>/<year> - <album>/ as "07 - Title [id].m4a" (the year first, so an
artist's albums sort oldest first wherever they are listed by name; an album without a year, its
title alone): "2-07 - ..." on an album of more than one disc, three digits on an album of 100
tracks or more, so a folder's names sort in track order. Names are cut to 180 bytes and folders to
100, and the characters a FAT card refuses (< > : " / \ | ? * and control characters, a trailing
dot or space) are replaced. Off: every song in Apple Music/ itself as "Title - Artist [id].m4a".

Either way the [id] at the end of a name is how q2-applemusic knows a song is on the card: it reads
Apple Music/ and the folders under it (hidden ones skipped) at its start, and again, in the
background, when the page asks for a list a minute or more after the last read, so songs moved by
hand within Apple Music/ are found. The start's read comes after the page's socket is up, in one
pass that also sweeps temp files left behind: Q2 Pod gives a starting app 10 s to answer
(ADDON_START_MS) and stops it after, and a card of thousands of songs, read cold after a boot, took
longer than that (v1.4 and before read it twice first, so a full card could never start). Until
the read is done, Downloaded Songs says "Reading the card…" and nothing downloads; a song queued
meanwhile that turns out to be on the card is skipped.

The song under way is counted in queue.json before it starts and the count taken back when it
returns, so only a death of q2-applemusic under way (killed, out of memory, a crash) leaves it
counted: one counted three times goes to the failed songs ("it stopped Apple Music each time")
instead of first again after every restart. The temp files an interrupted download left are swept
when q2-applemusic starts.

Deezer's duplicates (dedupe.go)
-------------------------------

After the start's read of the card, and each time the queue empties having downloaded something,
Deezer/<artist>/<album>/ (q2-deezer's organized folders) is compared with Apple Music/<artist>/<album>/
and 48khz/<artist>/<album>/ (Playlists/ aside): an album is its artist folder's name (letters and
digits, lower case) and its title (albumKey: the year before or after, bracketed editions and
" - EP" or " - Single" left out, letters and digits only; equal, not one within the other), and its
songs are counted. A Deezer album Apple Music has at least as many songs of gets a .nomedia whose
text is ourMark; one of ours whose album no longer matches loses it; any other .nomedia is left.
Q2 Pod's library scan skips a folder holding .nomedia (its ringnav_scan_dir). Downloaded Songs says
how many are kept out.

Stream mode
-----------

Mode: Stream (.applemusic/mode "stream"; Download is the default): a press on a song plays it and
the rest of its list after it, Play All the list from its start, and nothing is kept in Apple Music/.
A session is a folder, .applemusic/stream/<seq>/ (seq: the start's time in ms), holding the list's
songs from the pressed one, at most 200, named in play order ("01 - Title [id].m4a", three digits
for 100 or more), each fetched, decrypted and tagged as a download is (a song already downloaded is
copied from Apple Music/ instead). /tmp/q2-applemusic.play names the session, "<seq> <folder>". Q2
Pod plays the folder from its first song once one is there, adds each later song to the end of that
queue as it comes, and writes the path of the song playing to /tmp/q2-applemusic.playing. The
session fetches up to two songs past that one, then waits for the Q2 to move on, deleting songs more
than five before the one playing; it ends after an hour without the Q2 moving on. A new session
first moves in the old sessions' songs it needs, renamed, and deletes the old ones. A song Apple
won't send is left out; one that fails for the network is tried again (every 5 s, up to five
times). .applemusic is a hidden folder, which Q2 Pod's library scan skips, so streamed songs never
join the Library.
